========================================================================
(A) DELETION LADDER  u(n) <= floor(n*u(n-1)/(n-2))  from u(22)<=61
========================================================================
  n   3n ladder bd AMP cited  match? L(n) constr
 22   66        61        61    True          60
 23   69        66        66    True          64
 24   72        72        72    True          68
 25   75        78        78    True          72
 26   78        84        84    True          76
 27   81        90        90    True          81

  ALL AMP bounds (n=23..27) == deletion ladder from u(22)<=61 ?  True
  => only u(21)=57 (exact) and u(22)<=61 need heavy machinery;
     the entire ladder above 22 is elementary averaging.

  ladder from u(21)=57 gives u(22) <= 62  (AMP's 61 is 1 sharper)

========================================================================
(B) FLOOR ADVANCEMENT THRESHOLDS  (exact-integer)
========================================================================
  u(25) <= 3*25=75  via averaging  <==  u(24) <= 69   [check floor(25*69/23)=75 <= 75: True];  construction L(24)=68  gap=1
  u(26) <= 3*26=78  via averaging  <==  u(25) <= 72   [check floor(26*72/24)=78 <= 78: True];  construction L(25)=72  gap=0
  u(27) <= 3*27=81  via averaging  <==  u(26) <= 75   [check floor(27*75/25)=81 <= 81: True];  construction L(26)=76  gap=-1

  Interpretation:
  * u(24) <= 69  ==> u(25) <= 75 = 3*25  (floor advances to N*>=26).
    Construction L(24)=68, AMP bound 72; truth in [68,72]; need <=69.
  * u(25) <= 72  ==> u(26) <= 78 = 3*26  (=> N*>=27).  L(25)=72 (tight!).
  * u(26) <= 78  ==> u(27) <= 81 = 3*27  (=> N*>=28, settling u(27)=81).
    L(26)=76; need <=78.

  Even the OPTIMISTIC anchor u(22)=60 (=construction) propagates to:
    u(25) <= 76   (3n=75;  beats 3n floor? True)
    u(26) <= 82   (3n=78;  beats 3n floor? True)
    u(27) <= 88   (3n=81;  beats 3n floor? True)
  => averaging from n=22 CANNOT reach 3n at 25/26/27 (blocked by L(22)>=60).
  => advancing the floor REQUIRES a non-averaging (geometric) bound at
     one of n in {24,25,26} -- the targets are only 1-3 below current bds.

========================================================================
(C) TRIPLE CONFLUENCE AT n=27 = 3^3
========================================================================
  kissing number of the plane kappa = 6,  kappa/2 = 3
  3n  at n=27         = 81
  n^(4/3) at n=27     = 81   (exact: 27^(4/3)=(3^3)^(4/3)=3^4)
  3^4                 = 81
  3^(kappa/2)         = 27   (size of triangle-cube K3^[]^3)
  (kappa/2)^3         = 27   (crossover of line 3n and curve n^4/3)
  line 3n = curve n^(4/3)  <==>  n^(1/3) = kappa/2 = 3  <==>  n = 27
  FIXED-POINT: 3^(kappa/2) == (kappa/2)^3 holds because kappa/2 = 3.
  All four benchmarks (cube tie, incidence crossover, 3^4, 3*27) = 81 at 27.

  sign of (3n)^3 - n^4  (=27 n^3 - n^4 = n^3(27-n)):  >0 for n<27, =0 at 27, <0 n>27
    n=24: (3n)^3-n^4 =    41472  => 3n > n^(4/3)
    n=25: (3n)^3-n^4 =    31250  => 3n > n^(4/3)
    n=26: (3n)^3-n^4 =    17576  => 3n > n^(4/3)
    n=27: (3n)^3-n^4 =        0  => 3n = n^(4/3)
    n=28: (3n)^3-n^4 =   -21952  => 3n < n^(4/3)
    n=29: (3n)^3-n^4 =   -48778  => 3n < n^(4/3)

DONE.
